{"id":"coffee-countries","title":"Countries that produce the most coffee","prompt":"Name the 10 countries that grow the most coffee (FAO, 2023)","noun":"countries","category":"Business","metric":"Green coffee (2023)","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of countries by coffee production","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_coffee_production","asOf":"2026-11-04","dataAsOf":"2023"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Brazil","aliases":["Republic of Brazil","Brésil","Federative Republic of Brazil","Federal Republic of Brazil","Brasil","República Federativa do Brasil","Brazilian Federative Republic","Barzil","Brzil","Brazl","Brazilian Republic","Brasile","Brazzil","Brazilian"],"value":"3,405,267 tonnes","n":3405267,"article":"Brazil","fact":{"text":"Its first coffee bush was planted in Pará in 1727; today it grows about a third of the world's coffee.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_production_in_Brazil"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Vietnam","aliases":["Socialist Republic of Vietnam","Vietnarm","SRVN","Yuenan","Veitnam","Vietman","Viet Nam Socialist Repub","Socialist Republic of Viet Nam","Yue Nan","Red Vietnam","SRoV","SR Vietnam","CHXHCN Vietnam","People's Republic of Vietnam","CHXHCNVN","Vietnamese Socialist Republic","Vetnam","An Nam","Betonamu","Viet Nam","Vietnamese"],"value":"1,956,782 tonnes","n":1956782,"article":"Vietnam","fact":{"text":"French missionaries are believed to have brought the coffee plant here in 1857.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_production_in_Vietnam"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Indonesia","aliases":["Republic of Indonesia","Indonisia","Indnonesia","Indonnesia","Republik Indonesia","Unitary State of Republic of Indonesia","Indoneshia","Indonesian Republic","Yinni","Idnonesia","NKRI","Indinesia","Idonesia","Indonesian"],"value":"760,192 tonnes","n":760192,"article":"Indonesia","fact":{"text":"In 1711 the Dutch East India Company shipped the first coffee from Java to Europe.","source":"https://en.wikipedi